{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"b10344da-6e47-441d-b155-7481c9875c8d","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The causes for the silent nightly launchd job failures have been identified, the files fixed, and details documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-9Rj4op/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Causes\n1. **Missing `USER` environment variable in launchd context (`Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist`)**:\n   Under launchd's minimal environment, `USER` was not defined. The `claude` CLI failed to access keychain login credentials, printing `Not logged in · Please run /login` and exiting with code 1.\n2. **Assigning to read-only variable `status` in zsh (`bin/nightly-review.zsh`)**:\n   Line 19 attempted `status=$?`. In `zsh`, `status` is a read-only alias for `$?`. Attempting to assign to it resulted in a fatal script crash (`read-only variable: status`) before `bin/notify.sh` could be called.\n\n### Summary of Fixes Applied\n- **[com.vk.nightly-review.plist](file:///tmp/h-9Rj4op/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist)**: Added `\u003ckey\u003eUSER\u003c/key\u003e\u003cstring\u003evk\u003c/string\u003e` under `EnvironmentVariables`.\n- **[nightly-review.zsh](file:///tmp/h-9Rj4op/bin/nightly-review.zsh)**:\n  - Changed `status=$?` and its subsequent references to `rc=$?`.\n  - Added `\u003c /dev/null` to the `claude -p` invocation to prevent any potential stdin hangs under launchd.\n- **[ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-9Rj4op/ANSWER.md)**: Documented the root causes, fixes, and which parts of the colleague's notes applied versus which were ignored.\n","duration_seconds":51.602195,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":161168,"output_tokens":2178,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":0,"total_tokens":163346}}}
